T[3727]=dict(
title="Hike and Bike Morocco: Climb Toubkal and Ride the Agafay Desert",
ov=["This tour starts and ends in Marrakech and packs a lot into eight days. First you trek for three days through the Azaden and Imnan valleys to the top of Toubkal (4,167 m), the highest peak in North Africa. Then you swap boots for a bike and ride two days through the Ouirgane valley and out into the stony Agafay desert.",
    "The trek is challenging and the cycling is moderate. Mules carry the bags in the mountains, and a 4x4 supports you on the bike days."],
facts=[("Tour name","Hike and Bike Morocco"),("Duration","8 days: 3 days trekking and 2 days cycling"),("Grade","Challenging trek, moderate cycling"),("Best time to visit","March to November"),("Bike","Gravel bike, mountain bike or e-bike"),("Group size","2 to 16 people"),("Recommended age","16 to 65"),("Start / finish","Marrakech"),("Accommodation","Hotels, camps and guesthouses (gîtes)")],
inc=["Meals: 7 breakfasts, 5 lunches and 5 dinners, plus mineral water","All meals during the tour except dinner on day 1 and day 7 in Marrakech","Accommodation: 2 nights in hotels, 2 nights in guesthouses and 3 nights in camps","Rooms are twin share; a single room is available for a supplement of 450 EUR","Transport by comfortable van or Toyota Land Cruiser (4x4), including airport transfers on day 1 and day 8","A 4x4 support vehicle with the riders every day","2 days of guided cycling and 3 days of guided trekking","Visit of Jemaa el-Fna square and the old medina of Marrakech","The climb of Toubkal, the highest peak in North Africa","A night in the Agafay desert"],
exc=["Flights","Visas","Meals not listed in the itinerary","Tips","Alcoholic drinks","Laundry and souvenirs","Personal travel insurance","Bike hire (mountain bike, gravel bike or e-bike). You can bring your own bike or rent one from us."],
hl=["Explore the old medina of Marrakech","Hike and bike in the Atlas Mountains","Climb Toubkal, the highest peak in North Africa","Trek through the Imnan and Azaden valleys","Ride through Ouirgane and the Agafay desert"],
it={1:("Arrival in Marrakech","We meet you at Marrakech Menara Airport and drive you to your hotel, 15 minutes away. Later you meet your guide for a briefing. If you have time, visit the old town, Bahia Palace and Jemaa el-Fna square."),
2:("Marrakech to the Tamsoult valley","After breakfast we drive about two hours to Imlil, where the trek starts. We meet the muleteers and walk for five hours over the Tizi Mzik pass (2,489 m / 8,166 ft), then down to our camp in the Tamsoult valley."),
3:("Tamsoult to the Toubkal refuge","A steady climb on an old mule path brings us to the Aguelzim pass (3,550 m), with a superb view of the Toubkal massif. After a picnic we go down to the refuge (3,207 m) and camp for the night."),
4:("Toubkal summit (4,167 m) and Aremd","Summit day. We start early and reach the top of Toubkal in about three and a half hours. On a clear day you can see for miles in every direction. After some time on the summit we go back down to the refuge for lunch, then continue to Aremd for a night in a guesthouse."),
5:("Aremd to Ouirgane via the Imnan valley","Now the bikes come out. We roll down to Imlil, then climb to the Tizi n'Tamatert pass (2,380 m) through the Berber villages of Ikiss and Tinghrin. Lunch is in the Imnan valley, with its terraced fields. After lunch a long, fun descent takes us to Asni, and a short transfer brings us to our guesthouse in the Ouirgane valley.<br><strong>Note:</strong> If you want more riding, you can cycle the extra 18 km to the guesthouse."),
6:("Ouirgane and the Agafay desert","A short climb to the Tizi Ouadou pass (1,276 m) warms the legs, and we enjoy the view with a glass of mint tea. Then we ride down the valley to the Lalla Takerkoust lake for lunch by the water. In the afternoon we ride the last section into the Agafay desert and spend the night in a comfortable desert camp."),
7:("Agafay to Marrakech","After breakfast we drive back to Marrakech for a city tour with a local guide: Bahia Palace, the Koutoubia mosque and the lanes of the old medina, ending at Jemaa el-Fna square."),
8:("Departure","Transfer to Menara Airport for your flight. Check-out is at 11:30. We hope to see you again soon – ma'a salama!")})
T[3656]=dict(
title="Hiking in the Ait Bouguemez Valley: Land of the Berbers",
ov=["The Ait Bouguemez, better known as the Happy Valley, is a green valley about 30 km long in the central High Atlas, around 210 km east of Marrakech. Berber villages sit between the fields, and above them rises M'Goun, at over 4,070 m the second-highest mountain in Morocco.",
    "This is a gentle trek. You walk four to five hours a day from village to village and sleep in family-run guesthouses, while mules carry the bags. You also visit the Ouzoud waterfalls and the natural bridge of Imi n'Ifri on the way."],
facts=[("Tour name","Hiking in the Ait Bouguemez Valley"),("Duration","8 days, 7 nights, 5 days of trekking"),("Grade","Easy"),("Best time to visit","March to October"),("Type of travel","Trekking"),("Group size","2 to 16 people"),("Recommended age","8 to 80"),("Start / finish","Marrakech"),("Accommodation","Guesthouses and a hotel or riad")],
inc=["Meals: 7 breakfasts, 7 lunches and 6 dinners, plus mineral water during the trek","Accommodation: 2 nights in a hotel and 5 nights in guesthouses","Transport by comfortable van or 4x4, plus mules and muleteers during the trek","A walk at the Ouzoud waterfalls, 5 days of trekking in the Ait Bouguemez valley and a visit to the natural bridge of Imi n'Ifri"],
exc=["Flights","Visas","Meals not listed in the itinerary","Tips, drinks, laundry and souvenirs","Personal travel insurance"],
hl=["Wander the lanes of the old medina of Marrakech","Five days of walking in the Happy Valley","Stay with Berber families in village guesthouses","See the Ouzoud waterfalls","Visit the natural bridge of Imi n'Ifri"],
it={1:("Arrival in Marrakech","Welcome to Marrakech, the Red City. Look for the We Gravel Morocco sign at Menara Airport, and we'll drive you to your hotel. Explore the city if you like, but be back for the welcome meeting, where your guide goes through the trip."),
2:("Marrakech to the Happy Valley via the Ouzoud waterfalls","After breakfast we drive about five and a half hours to the valley, passing through Azilal and stopping at the Ouzoud waterfalls. In the Happy Valley we meet the muleteers and walk for an hour to our guesthouse."),
3:("To Ait Imi and the Sidi Moussa granary","A 4–5 hour walk through the heart of the valley. We climb up to Sidi Moussa, an old hilltop granary where families kept their grain in small rooms. In the afternoon we walk up the valley from village to village to our guesthouse in Ait Imi."),
4:("Ait Imi to Zaouit Oulmzi","We walk through the village of Ibaqalliwn to see dinosaur footprints left in the rock millions of years ago. Then we continue to Adazen for a great view of the valley. After lunch we go down to Zaouit Oulmzi for the night."),
5:("Zaouit Oulmzi to Ikhf n'Ighir","We follow the wide, green Ait Hakim valley through a string of traditional villages. Lunch is in the shade of big walnut trees, then we walk on to Ikhf n'Ighir for dinner and the night."),
6:("Ikhf n'Ighir to Agouti","Our last day of walking crosses the villages of Ait Ziri and Aguerd n'Ouzrou and the Tamzrit plateau, with wide views over the whole valley. Along the way you'll meet farmers in the fields and women washing clothes in the river, and see how the valley's people live from the land."),
7:("Agouti to Marrakech via Imi n'Ifri","After breakfast we drive about five hours back to Marrakech, stopping at the natural bridge of Imi n'Ifri. Night in a hotel or riad."),
8:("Departure","Transfer to the airport for your flight home.")})
T[3627]=dict(
title="Toubkal Trek and Essaouira: 7 Days from Marrakech",
ov=["Mountains first, then the sea. On this 7-day trip you trek for three days to the summit of Toubkal (4,167 m), the highest peak in North Africa. Then you spend two relaxed days in Essaouira, a laid-back fishing town on the Atlantic with a UNESCO-listed medina. The trip ends with a guided day in Marrakech.",
    "It's a good way to earn your beach time. The climb is hard work, and the ocean breeze in Essaouira feels well deserved afterwards."],
facts=[("Tour name","Toubkal Trek and Essaouira"),("Duration","7 days, 6 nights, 3 days of trekking"),("Grade","Moderate to hard"),("Best time to visit","March to November"),("Type of travel","Trekking and relaxing"),("Group size","2 to 16 people"),("Recommended age","16 to 70"),("Start / finish","Marrakech"),("Accommodation","Guesthouse, camp and riad or hotel")],
inc=["Meals: 6 breakfasts, 2 lunches and 2 dinners, plus mineral water during the trek","Accommodation: 4 nights in hotels, 1 night in a guesthouse and 1 night in a camp","Transport by comfortable van or 4x4, plus mules and muleteers during the trek","The guided climb of Toubkal, a guided tour of Essaouira and a guided tour of Marrakech"],
exc=["Flights","Visas","Meals not listed in the itinerary","Tips, drinks, laundry and souvenirs","Personal travel insurance"],
hl=["Trek through the Imnan valley","Climb the highest peak in North Africa","Explore the souks of Marrakech","Relax in the seaside town of Essaouira"],
it={1:("Arrival in Marrakech","Welcome to Marrakech, the Red City. Look for the We Gravel Morocco sign at Menara Airport, and we'll drive you to your hotel. Explore the city if you like before the welcome meeting, where you meet your guide and go through the trip."),
2:("Marrakech to Imlil (1,750 m) and the Toubkal refuge (3,207 m)","After breakfast we drive an hour and a half to Imlil. We meet the muleteers and climb steadily on a mule path to the shrine of Sidi Chamharouch (2,300 m), where we stop for a picnic. Then we continue to the Toubkal base camp (3,207 m). The walk takes about five and a half hours. You sleep in the refuge, or in a tent if you prefer, from May to the end of October."),
3:("Toubkal summit and Aremd","Summit day. We leave around 2:30 am to reach the top for the best light. It takes about three and a half hours from camp to the summit (4,167 m). After enjoying the view we go back down to camp for lunch, then continue to the village of Aremd for the night."),
4:("Aremd to Essaouira","A short walk takes us back to Imlil, then we travel to Essaouira on the Atlantic coast. The town used to be called Mogador. Its walled 18th-century medina is a UNESCO World Heritage Site and has long attracted artists."),
5:("Essaouira","A free day to enjoy Essaouira, with a guided walk included. Photograph the sea walls, a mix of Portuguese and Berber design, and browse the souks, woodworking shops and art galleries. At the harbour, stalls grill the fish that just came in. In the afternoon, walk on the beach or just relax."),
6:("Essaouira to Marrakech","We drive back to Marrakech for a guided city tour. You'll see Jemaa el-Fna square, the 12th-century Koutoubia mosque and the 19th-century Bahia Palace, have a traditional lunch and walk through the souks. The rest of the afternoon is free."),
7:("Departure","Transfer to the airport for your flight home.")})
